mc68000/
========

Musashi's sixty self-checking 68000 programs, the prebuilt test/mc68000/*.bin
of Musashi at commit 313ebf1bd9f4d0d93341eb5ce21fd8a119e9dbdd (2026-03-08),
copied unchanged. Each is linked at $10000 (test/entry.s), starts there with
its supervisor stack at $3F0, runs one family of instructions over many
values, compares checksums of the results and the flags with constants, and
writes a long to $100004 (TEST_PASS_REG) when they all match or to $100000
(TEST_FAIL_REG) at the first that does not, then stops with `stop #$2700`.
They are run by `musashi_programs_pass` in src/test/conformance.rs, through
Interpreter::from_image, and the ones left out are listed with their reasons
in src/conformance/skips.rs. Their sources, test/mc68000/*.s, are in
Musashi's repository and not here.

mc68040/
========

Seventeen of Musashi's eighteen self-checking programs of the 68040's integer
instructions, the prebuilt test/mc68040/*.bin of Musashi at the same commit,
313ebf1bd9f4d0d93341eb5ce21fd8a119e9dbdd, copied unchanged. They are built and
laid out as the mc68000 ones are, for a 68040 (test/mc68040/Makefile), and
cover the bit fields, cas and cas2, chk2 and cmp2, the long multiplies and
divides, trapcc, rtd, jmp and jsr, and shifts by a register. They are run by
`musashi_68040_programs_pass` in src/test/conformance.rs as 68020 Programs,
with the checks of the 68040's undefined flags relaxed and the ones not run
listed with their reasons in src/conformance/skips.rs. interrupt.bin is left
out: its interrupts come from a register of Musashi's test driver. Their
sources, test/mc68040/*.s, are in Musashi's repository and not here.

